.TH SSL 1.SH NAMEssl \- show a file's segment list.SH SYNOPSIS\fBssl\fRfile ....SH DESCRIPTION\fBssl\fRprints, for each file, the sector of its file descriptor and the list ofsegments the file occupies: each segment's starting sector and itslength in sectors..PPIts limits are its author's: the file must be named by its bare nameand be in the current directory -- a pathlist never matches, and it thenreports sector 0 and no segments -- and it reads the raw sectors of\fB/h0\fRwhatever device the file is on.  It wants the super user.\fBfstat \-s\fRshows the same list for any file, by pathlist..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOfstat, dam